# M4's done-when test: a self-test that retypes, revokes and retypes again
# gets the same result both times. Every call goes through l4core::invoke
# with CPtrs into the root CNode, as the root task will make them: the
# largest RAM untyped U is retyped into every object type, the CNode
# methods move capabilities between the root CNode and a new CNode (through
# its own capability and guarded copies), the new CNode also gets copies of
# the BootInfo frame and the root CNode capability, which only its Zombie
# can delete, the untyped made from U is retyped too, and three calls fail
# as they must. Every slot is recorded, the objects are filled, U is
# revoked, and the same calls run again: the record must match and the
# objects read zero, or as retype makes them. After each revoke every slot
# the test filled is empty,
# the boot capabilities are roots without links again (but for the root
# TCB's copies of root slots 2, 3 and 10), and every slot
# passes cdt::check_slot. The kernel waits for a timer interrupt before
# run 1, so the first reset of U is preempted by it at its first poll;
# injected preemptions hit both runs and both revokes. Every call restarts
# from the idle path; the kernel counts and checks the restarts. Each
# phase reports its preemptions and the stretches between its polls.
cmdline: test=retype
exit: success
expect: microL4 kernel
expect: cmdline: "test=retype"
expect: bootinfo: boot region
expect: retype: U is root slot
expect: retype: an interrupt is pending, so run 1's reset of U is preempted by it at its first poll
expect: retype: run 1: U into a 1 MiB untyped preempted by an interrupt at poll 1 (attempt 1)
expect: retype: run 1 done:
expect: retype: run 1: preempted
expect: retype: revoke 1 done: the 26 slots the test filled are empty, C's copies of root slots 9 and 2 included; U and the boot capabilities are as run 1 left them, roots without links but the root TCB's copies
expect: retype: revoke 1: preempted
expect: retype: run 2 done: the same
expect: its objects' 2067 KiB read zero, or as retype makes them # frames, TCBs' registers and XSAVE areas, PML4s' upper back-references
expect: retype: run 2: preempted
expect: retype: revoke 2 done: the 26 slots the test filled are empty, C's copies of root slots 9 and 2 included
expect: retype: revoke 2: preempted
expect: restarts from the idle path after
expect: retype: the longest stretch between two polls:
expect: TEST PASS
